From 9e66aa7bb6fc573ef595bdf1b89701e3d7f0574f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FrankX3M <you@example.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 16:28:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: call init_db() on app startup; fix xcaddy/Go install;
 add caddy systemd unit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

src/main.py: switch to FastAPI lifespan, call core.db.session.init_db() on
startup. Root cause of the deploy-time crash:

  sqlalchemy.exc.OperationalError: (sqlite3.OperationalError) no such table: server_config

init_db() existed and worked correctly (Base.metadata.create_all), but was
never called anywhere outside of test fixtures that build their own in-memory
engine. The module-level comment claiming this was intentional (deferred to
an undefined 'deployment step') was incorrect — there is no such step in the
pipeline, and the panel crashed on every first request against a fresh DB.

deploy/install.sh:
  - install a Go toolchain before  (xcaddy compiles Caddy from
    source and needs Go on PATH; previously failed with
    'exec: "go": executable file not found in $PATH')
  - install xcaddy via the Cloudsmith apt repo instead of the old
    raw.githubusercontent.com/.../xcaddy/master/install.sh, which now 404s
  - make the sing-box / xcaddy / caddy steps idempotent (skip if already
    installed) so the script is safe to re-run

deploy/systemd/caddy.service (new):
  building Caddy via  (required for the forwardproxy/naive
  module) does not ship a systemd unit or a 'caddy' system user the way the
  official apt package does — both are created explicitly now.

tests/test_app_startup.py (new):
  regression test for the init_db() bug. Spawns the app in a subprocess with
  cwd = repo root (mirrors the systemd WorkingDirectory in production) and
  asserts all five tables exist after the lifespan startup/shutdown cycle.
  Existing API tests didn't catch this because their TestClient fixture
  builds tables directly against an in-memory engine, bypassing the app's
  own startup path entirely.

All checks green: ruff, mypy --ignore-missing-imports, pytest (85 passed).
